<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Helos</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Helos was an ancient town in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laconia">Laconia</a>, in the marshy plain near the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eurotas">Eurotas</a> river, mentioned in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/homer">Homer</a>'s Catalogue of Ships. Ancient tradition derived the name of the helots, the state serfs of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a>, from its inhabitants, said to have been enslaved after resisting the Spartans. In the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> Slavic settlers known as the Ezeritai lived in the plain.</p></div>
